VALUES (586, 'J3', $t$ASK 586 J3: a judge's break that says a side granted something names the grant from THE GRANTS LISTS; a record-only check (E-GRT) sends a faulty line back once$t$,
  $t$A judge's break line that says a side granted, conceded, dropped or withdrew something names the grant by its number from THE GRANTS LISTS, which serve each side's own grant sentences from the rounds, or says NOT A LISTED GRANT and quotes that side's words with their round; a line that does neither goes back once; the judge keeps the decision (ruling 428); the lists are the sides' own sentences (rulings 382 and 383). (Plan ask586/w3/plan586.md rev 6 section 4A, J3; texts ask586/w3/texts586_J2J3J6.md section 2; W4's notes_j3.md; the operator's press "Write J3, not counted".)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write J3, not counted" at 09:16 CST 2026-11-24 (Wall 11552; audit 41457). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 347f3e21 to 137378eb-c1b1-45ab-ab87-0febeab23ac6 (423 nodes); child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT e086bb3a to ecdc6218-834d-4658-a90d-088414a22fa3 (156 nodes). Base E (ASK 591 live). LIB 47a39128fec62d31, MAP efe8431fb6af14e1. OPTION A is live: an uncured E-GRT item is recorded and counts against no seat. Option B (counted) is not built. What changed, every change an insertion (W1's walk, Wall 11509): (1) the judges' text gains, once in each judge's request, after "A shown chain is footing only through its rows and what the other side has granted (pkgBCL).", the paragraph on THE GRANTS LISTS, G<n> and NOT A LISTED GRANT (Panel Build; Build Independent Verdict the same text, and that node does not run). (2) Panel Build gathers THE GRANTS LISTS from both sides' rounds by a copy of the engine's own grants harvester (no 260 or 160 cut; a bare grant served with the line before it; one numbering, the defender's first) and serves the block once per judge request, directly above the COLLISION POINTS instructions; when gathering fails the block reads "not available this run" and the check does nothing. (3) Shared Library, engine and child: line 3564 gains the check (rule E-GRT, faults 1, 2 and 3, the judge's whole line stored); lines 2784, 2789, 2929 and 2959 carry the record (never counted as silence; the row reads "GRANT NOT NAMED (E-GRT, ASK 586 J3, fault n): record-only, counts against no seat; the judge keeps the decision (ruling 428)"). No setting changes; nothing deleted. Three builds of the one change: rev 0 on bases A and B (Wall 11508; W1 PASS with R1, Wall 11509); a re-cut on the J2 base with one build anchor changed and the inserted text unchanged (Wall 11525; W1 PASS, Wall 11528); a re-cut on the ASK 591 base, whose three node texts and child equal the J2-based target byte for byte (Wall 11548; W1 PASS, Wall 11549). The last is what was written. W1's R1 (Wall 11509), on the card: the send-back builders stop with "no enforcer reported a violation in a panel judge line" before line 3564, so an E-GRT item reaches a judge only on a pass that already holds an enforcer item; in the last 30 days that stop was met on 14 of 123 panel passes and 22 of 72 alternate passes (notes_j2.md, notes_j3.md; card586j3.md words it "14 of 123 runs had a panel pass"). Moving the stop is offered as its own ASK. C7 measure on stored judgments 1263 to 1274 (4 runs; out_c7.txt): 67 break lines; 4 would go back, all fault 1; none uses a grant word for something other than a grant; one (1270) names no side and the side is taken from the broken link. Run 42071: 2 of 13; the judge request grows by 2,323 characters (defender none, challenger 13 sentences); nothing is capped. LIMITS, stated: an E-GRT item asks for no FORCED-line companion; the check's reader ends [DR4] at the end of the user text, so fault 3 is lenient for words in text appended after it; no code decides whether a judge is right to read words as a grant. IN PART, because no run has executed on 137378eb or a later version (debate_results last row 21:57 CST 2026-11-23, run 42071): the text, the block, the check and the record are shown by t_j3, by the end-to-end run on row 1274 and by the readback, not by a run. After this write ASK 591 fix 1 was written on top (engine 6834c21b, Build Save Body only; Wall 11556, 11557). RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). THE GRANTS LISTS block reached the judges: sol62 and sol cite the grants by number (G1 to G6); chatgpt cites none. UNEXERCISED: the E-GRT check and its send-back (no E-GRT row; W3 found no break line that rests on a grant word). In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
